==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|letter box}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|letter|box}}
[[File:Letterboxes Ocotillo Wells 2013.jpg|thumb|Letterboxes next to a stop sign in California]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|Irish}} A box into which [[mail]] is put.
#: {{syn|en|mailbox|q=chiefly US}}
## A collection point for mail intended for onward delivery, a [[secure]] [[box]] or [[receptacle]] for this purpose.
##: {{syn|en|post box|pillar box|q2=UK}}
## A delivery point for mail, a [[box]], [[compartment]] or [[slot]] for this purpose.
##: {{syn|en|mail slot|q=US}}
##: {{uxi|en|A wad of junk mail was pushed through the '''letterbox''' in the front door and dropped onto the mat.}}
# A [[hidden]] [[container]] that holds a [[logbook]] and [[rubber stamp]], found by following [[clue]]s as a form of [[recreation]].
# {{lb|en|mountaineering}} A [[rectangular]] [[hole]] or [[slot]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1954|author=Daniel Talbot|title=A Treasury of Mountaineering Stories|page=239
|passage=His strength was running out fast: one more good '''letterbox''' was all that he could conceive himself able to make. He made it, hacking away with slow, painful strokes, his axe-handle slippery with his sweat.}}

